    "created_at": "2016-11-19T16:01:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-19T16:01:27Z",
    "body": "> It adds more semantics\n\nWhat semantics would it add, exactly? That is, can you name any existing semantic analysis tools (search engines, etc.) which are excited to take advantage of the new grouping information you propose? It seems like instead you would want such tools to ignore such grouping information, like they do today with div and span.\n\n> It helps styling\n\nYou can in fact use div to group the children of dl, so this argument doesn't seem to hold.\n\n> It is optional\n\nThis is not an argument for adding something. See https://wiki.whatwg.org/wiki/FAQ#Where.27s_the_harm_in_adding.E2.80.94\n\n> Postscript\n\nAs presented, div and span are exactly correct for this use case. You don't want to introduce new semantic meaning here; that would just confuse existing tools for no benefit. And they can in fact pass conformance checkers in the dl case. Try it out: https://checker.html5.org/#textarea\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
